{
  "description": "Held-out Java CALLS set (#177): 60 call sites of spring-framework v7.1.0 drawn at random from the production sources by `sample_java_sites.py --heldout` (seed 4177) after the resolver was frozen, each traced to its targets by reading the code at the pinned commit, never from myceliums output, and scored once. The headline Java numbers. Reported by graph-eval, never gated.",
  "role": "held-out",
  "labelled_by": "agent",
  "reviewed_by": null,
  "rules": "Sites are drawn by `sample_java_sites.py --heldout` (seed 4177, the `random` stratum only: call-looking tokens drawn uniformly from the production sources) after the resolver was frozen (commit 37b1443 of #177; no resolver change after the draw), and read in the order of the draw; the first 60 that qualify are taken. A site whose (file, caller, callee) pair is in the dev set is skipped. A site is skipped when it is not a call made inside a named method or constructor (a declaration, an annotation, a string, a comment, a field initialiser, an abstract or interface method declaration), when it repeats a pair already taken,. The caller is the innermost named method or constructor containing the call, including methods of anonymous classes and enum constant bodies; calls in lambdas belong to the enclosing method. A pair lists every project symbol the caller's calls of that name bind to under javac's rules: the declaration of the receiver's static type (inherited declarations where the class does not declare it; the overload javac selects) and, where the call dispatches, every override of it in the repository (found by git grep over the subtypes). `new X(...)` targets the class X and its matching constructor. An empty list means no call of that name in the caller binds to a project symbol: a JDK or library method, a method inherited from a library base class, an implicit member with no declaration (a record accessor). Annotation elements (`ann.value()`) are interface methods and are targets. `inner-anonymous` is set mechanically: the caller's declaration is indented two levels or more (spring-framework indents with tabs).",
  "fetch": "crates/myceliums-benchmarks/graph-gold/held-out/fetch_java.sh",
  "repos": {
    "spring-framework": "f2e4863de60e6a20e827a0aa3c524ffb3ae96ad4"
  },
  "report_only": [],
  "cases": {
    "dispatch": "the call goes through an interface or abstract (or overridden) method: the declaration the receiver's static type binds, plus every override in the repository",
    "overload": "the callee name has several overloads in view; the target is the one javac picks (arity alone may not decide)",
    "generics": "the receiver's type comes from a type argument (List<DataBuffer>.get(0)) or a type-parameter bound (C extends X)",
    "inner-anonymous": "the caller is a method of a nested, inner, local or anonymous class (enum constant bodies included)",
    "lambda": "the call is written inside a lambda body; it belongs to the enclosing method",
    "method-ref": "a method reference (Type::m, this::m). Not a call under the fixture rules (invokedynamic), so these pairs are reported apart and left out of the totals",
    "static-import": "a bare call bound by a static import of a project method (`import static org.springframework...`)",
    "injected-field": "the receiver is a field Spring injects (@Autowired, @Resource, @Inject, @MockitoBean) or a constructor-injected field",
    "inherited-library": "the class extends a library type and the call reaches a method inherited from it: no project target"
  },
